.TH DOZED 1
.SH NAME
dozed \- lightweight idle manager for Wayland compositors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dozed
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIevents...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dozed
listens for idle activity through the Wayland
.B ext-idle-notify-v1
protocol and executes configured commands. It can run against any compositor
that exposes the protocol.
.PP
.B dozed
is a fork of
.B swayidle.
The implementation has been largely rewritten, but the event model and much of
the behavior are inherited from swayidle.
.PP
dozed does not depend on systemd. If built with login1 D-Bus support, it can
also listen for sleep, resume, lock, and unlock events from a login1
implementation.
.PP
If the compositor exposes
.B zwlr_foreign_toplevel_manager_v1,
dozed will not execute idle timeout commands while any toplevel window is
fullscreen, unless
.B --ignore-fullscreen
or
.B --fullscreen-policy ignore
is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " path"
Use the specified config file.
.TP
.B \-h, --help
Show help and quit.
.TP
.B \-d
Enable debug output.
.TP
.B \-w
Wait for each command to finish before continuing.
.TP
.BI \-S " seat-name"
Specify which Wayland seat to use.
.TP
.B --no-config
Do not load any config file.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Validate configuration and command-line events, print the parsed events, and
exit without connecting to Wayland or running commands.
.TP
.B --validate-config
Validate configuration and command-line events, then exit.
.TP
.B --print-events
Print parsed events, then exit.
.TP
.B --ignore-fullscreen
Do not suppress idle timeout commands while a fullscreen app is active.
.TP
.BI --fullscreen-policy " suppress|ignore"
Choose fullscreen behavior. The default is
.BR suppress .
.SH EVENTS
.TP
.BI timeout " timeout command " [resume\  "resume-command" ]
Execute the timeout command if there is no activity for
.I timeout
seconds. If
.B resume
is specified, the resume command runs when activity resumes.
.TP
.BI before-sleep " command"
When built with login1 support, execute command before the system sleeps.
.TP
.BI after-resume " command"
When built with login1 support, execute command after the system resumes.
.TP
.BI lock " command"
When built with login1 support, execute command when the login1 session asks
the session to lock.
.TP
.BI unlock " command"
When built with login1 support, execute command when the login1 session asks
the session to unlock.
.PP
All commands are executed through
.BR "sh -c" .
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM, SIGINT
Run all pending resume commands and terminate.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Immediately enter idle state.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
dozed -w \\
	timeout 300 'swaylock -f -c 000000' \\
	timeout 600 'wlopm --off "*"' \\
		resume 'wlopm --on "*"' \\
	before-sleep 'swaylock -f -c 000000'
.fi
